; Install-script policy (npm >= 11.16, RFC npm/rfcs#868).
;
; npm resolves the effective policy from, highest precedence first:
;   1. --allow-scripts on the CLI  (an ERROR for project-scoped install/ci --
;      never pass it in CI)
;   2. the root package.json "allowScripts" field
;   3. this .npmrc
;
; The root package.json deliberately does not declare "allowScripts", so this
; file is the project's policy. If one is ever added there, npm ignores this
; layer entirely and logs a warning -- move the list, don't duplicate it.
;
; Why it is needed: better-sqlite3 is a native module and compiles (or fetches
; a prebuild) in its install script; esbuild and @swc/core unpack platform
; binaries. Today npm only *warns* about unreviewed install scripts, so `npm ci`
; would still work without this file -- but npm has announced that a future
; release blocks them by default, which would break CI and every fresh clone
; with no code change on our side. Declaring the list now is the cheap fix.
;
; Only bare package names are permitted here; semver ranges are rejected by npm
; (exact versions joined by "||" are the alternative). fsevents is macOS-only
; and inert on CI; it is listed so contributor machines match CI exactly.
;
; Not enabling strict-allow-scripts yet: it turns an unreviewed install script
; into a hard failure, and the dependency tree is not installed/audited yet.
; Turn it on as part of P9.1 release engineering, once `npm approve-scripts
; --allow-scripts-pending` reports clean.
allow-scripts=@swc/core,better-sqlite3,esbuild,fsevents
